## Now / next — Stage 4: the consumer-boundary eval unification (THE LINCHPIN)
The thesis (`homoiconic-unification.md` Stage 4 + Constructor face): **one eval = eval
DATA → runnable at EVERY consumer boundary.** Today three boundaries handle data→runnable
differently (or not at all) — unify them; *this is what dissolves the FLAT/RICH constructor
seam* (lets reaction/pattern constructors produce DATA like process/composite):
- [ ] **nodes** — `discover_processes` (`engine.rs:1486`/`:1449`): process-DATA spec → running
      node. EXISTS; expose as a first-class `.ys` `eval` (4a), unify with the `meta`-import
      `eval`/`load` (4b).
- [x] **rules** — `collect_reactions`/`push_reaction` (`brs.rs`): DONE (4c). `push_reaction`
      now evals a TRANSPARENT reaction-DATA map (`_pat="Rule"`) via the existing
      `ReactionRule::from_data_value`, additive beside the `Foreign` carrier — symmetric with
      `discover_processes`. Consumer: `prism-bigraph/tests/reaction_data_as_state.rs` (3 green).
      This is the substrate that lets `build_reaction_value` emit pure DATA (FLAT/RICH dissolves)
      + lets chrysalis's `ReactionType::realize` re-wrap retire (lang's flip, gated on this).
- [ ] **patterns** — `find_matches` (`prism_schema::reaction`): a `Pattern(…)`/redex DATA value
      → a matcher (4d).
- [ ] Unify the three as ONE "eval data→runnable" op/pattern. Thin-layer: chrysalis CALLS this;
      the eval lives HERE in core.

## Coordinate
`prism-schema` + `prism-bigraph` are SHARED crates everyone builds on — a public-API or
BRS/reaction-boundary change is **NON-MONOTONE** → **coordinate-FIRST** (read `board.ys`,
claim it in `touching`, drop a `note` so lang/domains rebuild). Gated on `lang`'s Stage-2b
completion (the reframe + param desugaring + uniformity proof) + `simplify`'s Stage-3 guard;
**prep now** — survey the three boundaries + design the unified op while lang finishes 2b.
Pair with `unify` on the design, `lang` on the chrysalis↔prism seam.

## Done (this arc)
- **Stage 4c (THE LINCHPIN)** — `push_reaction` (brs.rs) evals transparent reaction-DATA
  (`_pat="Rule"` map → `ReactionRule` via the existing `from_data_value`), additive beside the
  `Foreign` carrier. Tests: `reaction_data_as_state.rs` (3) + `rules_as_state` regression. The
  rule boundary now reads DATA like the node boundary (`discover_processes`).
- **`.ys` import grammar FLIPPED to explicit-origin** (user-chosen detour off the board work;
  see [[project_ys_import_explicit_origin]]): bare `from X import` = native/registry ONLY;
  sibling/relative file = `from .X import` (leading dot); package paths stay dotted. Collapsed
  `resolve_file_modules` to `is_file_module = module.contains('.')`, DELETED the `natives`
  precedence plumbing + `parse_file_with_natives` + `module_names()` (the retired #50). Migrated
  EVERY sibling import in the tree (coord board + `ys/` demos + spatio-flux `culture.ys`).
  `compile.rs` gives a `.X` migration hint on a bad bare import. Green across 10+ multi-file
  consumers + spatio-flux. Files: `parse.rs`, `compile.rs`, `cli.rs`, `spatio-flux/.../sf.rs`,
  `parse_import.rs`; GUIDE.md import section updated.
- **Two `.ys` board-robustness fixes** (the coord board dogfoods `.ys` as data): lexer now
  escapes a doubled quote `''` → `'` (unparse re-escapes) so heartbeat prose with apostrophes
  parses (was wedging the whole board via synth/unify/simplify); braces in prose are
  interpolation (avoid them; a `{{`-escape would harden it — flagged to lang).
- **`core` is ON the board** — `coord/core.ys` heartbeat created; `coord/board.ys` imports
  `.core` (the leading dot dodges the native-`core` collision). Full 6-peer board converges.
- **Recognition doc** — `schema-algebra.md` § "Eval: state-data → runnable (the lower rung)":
  the 3 boundaries (`discover_processes`/`collect_reactions`/`find_matches`) = ONE 2nd-rung eval,
  each an EXISTING op (not a new trait). `homoiconic-unification.md` 4c marked ✅ DONE + the lang
  handoff. Laws already pinned in `reaction_data.rs`.
- **Two Stage-4 core ENABLERS for lang (both green):**
  - **4a node rung** — `Core::instantiate_spec(spec) → ProcessNode` (`core.rs`): owns the
    `{_type,address,config}` envelope shape so chrysalis's surface `eval` CALLS it (thin-layer),
    never re-implementing the envelope. The node analogue of `from_data_value`/`Pattern::from_value`.
    Tests: `core.rs` `instantiate_spec_*` (2).
  - **Axis-A `type`-as-data** — `schema_codec::{schema_to_value,value_to_schema}` (already existed;
    now round-trip-pinned TOTAL over the user-`type` vocabulary incl. `Custom`, `schema_codec.rs`).
    Lang wires the `EntityDef` type arm to these. FINDING: units are NOT in the prism `Schema`
    (`Const`/`Quote` wrap an inner schema), so `unit`/`context` def-as-data is chrysalis AST
    serialization, not a core gap (units types lack serde — a gated add if lang's `UnitDef` needs it).

